Subject: [PATCH 08011/11362] [outer-loop] The unidentified leak route: one
 hardcoded sys.path insert poisons an entire xdist worker
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Docs only. Closes the open question left by the previous commit.

experiment_3351_gatemate_latency_benchmark.json leaked into the CANONICAL repo during a worktree run
even though its script resolves REPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] — correct and
repo-relative. The explanation matters more than the leak:

Three test files insert the HARDCODED canonical path straight onto sys.path —
  tests/python/test_arc3_gap3_stage2_ebm.py:14
    sys.path.insert(0, "/home/ianblenke/github.com/ianblenke/carnot/scripts/experiments")
  (also test_arc3_gap4_rule_exec.py, test_arc3_gap3_stage2v2_ebm.py)
and ten scripts under scripts/ do the equivalent with a hardcoded PROJECT_ROOT.

An xdist worker is a long-lived process running hundreds of test files in sequence. Once ANY of
those runs, the canonical tree is on that worker's sys.path for the rest of its life — so every
later `import experiment_NNNN` in that worker resolves to the CANONICAL module, its __file__ is the
canonical path, and a perfectly correct Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] then points at the
operator's checkout. A repo-relative script writes canonically through no fault of its own.

Consequence: worktree isolation is structurally defeated, per worker, by a single line in an
unrelated test. "Ran it in a worktree" is a mitigation, never containment; the load-bearing check is
a before/after hash of the canonical tree. This also raises the bar for repair option (F): fixing
the 139 hardcoded WRITE paths is necessary but not sufficient while hardcoded sys.path inserts
remain, because those re-import correct scripts from the wrong tree.

exp3734 leaked a second time during the whole-suite run and was again restored byte-identically.

